.yaml:24` matches `plan_review_findings` for removed symbol `plan_review_findings` but is not enumerated in the plan or file_impact","enumeration closure: `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-evidence-kind.eval.yaml:19` matches `plan_review_findings` for removed symbol `plan_review_findings` but is not enumerated in the plan or file_impact","enumeration closure: `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-finder.eval.yaml:20` matches `plan_review_findings` for removed symbol `plan_review_findings` but is not enumerated in the plan or file_impact","enumeration closure: 16 more un-enumerated path(s) match"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace the fresh-interpreter self-registration test with an in-process `monkeypatch.delitem(contracts._CONTRACTS, \"plan_review_findings\")` before scoring, then assert the score passes and the key is registered again. Drop the subprocess/portability note unless the test needs real interpreter isolation.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"measured: `import rebar` already imports `passes`, so it cannot be kept out of `sys.modules`\". The only state the test changes is the registry dict.","src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:25 `_CONTRACTS: dict[str, Callable[[], type]] = {}` is a plain module-level dict, so monkeypatch can delete the entry and restore it.","tests/unit/test_output_contract_no_reasoning_in_output.py:48 already reads `contracts._CONTRACTS` in-process, so tests already touch this registry directly."],"finding":"The self-registration test runs a fresh interpreter (`subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-c\", ...])`), but the plan's own measurement says `passes` is always already in `sys.modules`. The test therefore only removes `plan_review_findings` from the `contracts._CONTRACTS` dict, and an in-process `monkeypatch.delitem(contracts._CONTRACTS, \"plan_review_findings\")` does the same thing and restores the entry automatically. The subprocess adds interpreter-startup cost, a code-in-a-string test body, and the 'Portability: ... no shell' caveat, and isolates nothing extra.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbe351c0b6aa7dd36","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing → self-registration bullet; Scope → Portability note; AC2","norm_id":"nb0c9e8dbd3764ba5","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The unit suite pays a full `import rebar` interpreter startup for an assertion that needs no isolation.","A failure inside the `-c` string shows up as an opaque subprocess return code or stderr instead of a normal pytest assertion diff."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py: `monkeypatch.delitem(contracts._CONTRACTS, \"plan_review_findings\")`, then `res = score(\"emits_valid_findings\", case, {\"findings\": [{\"finding\": \"x\", \"criteria\": [\"G7\"]}]})`, then `assert res.passed and \"plan_review_findings\" in contracts._CONTRACTS`. Update AC2's wording from 'fresh-interpreter test' to match.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the discovery root and filter for the parametrized test (e.g. the packaged spec directory plus `_criterion_id(spec) is not None`), and state that the seven-spec set was enumerated statically from that root (or replace the exact-equality check with a superset check).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2","E6","COH"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7371,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"parametrized over packaged criterion-id specs listing `emits_valid_findings`; first assert the discovered set is exactly the seven above\"","Root cause says other consumers are also criterion-id specs: \"`evals/plan-review-gate/fixtures/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml`, `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-*.eval.yaml` (dotted `project.*` ids), and specs generated by `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_emit.py`\"","The seven were observed as failing in a live run at `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12`. A spec whose sampled cases never fired would not appear in that list. Nothing states the seven were enumerated statically."],"finding":"The happy-path test parametrizes over 'packaged criterion-id specs listing emits_valid_findings' and asserts the discovered set is 'exactly the seven above'. 'Packaged' is undefined, and the exact-seven claim is unsupported.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb1a8049f5d6ccd3b","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — happy path bullet; Acceptance Criteria #1","norm_id":"ne19942e45c093d4a","priority":0.0629,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor discovers from a root that also includes the gate fixtures or .rebar/evals specs. The count is not seven, and they cannot tell whether the test or the plan is wrong.","A packaged criterion-id spec lists emits_valid_findings but had no fired case in the live sample. The exact-set assertion then fails on the first run."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In the attribution test, name the exact spec id passed to `run_case` for the G3 container case and the FakeRunner findings it fires (e.g. `[{\"finding\": \"x\", \"criteria\": [\"G3\"]}]`).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`run_case(\"G3\", <first G3 must-fire case of the packaged container spec, which carries `children`>)`\"","Repro: \"`run_case(\"plan-review-G7\", <G7 must-fire case>, runner=FakeRunner(...))`\"","\"plan-review-container ... raise \\\"no eval solver\\\" today (`eval_solver.py:423`)\", so the container spec name cannot be used as the solver target."],"finding":"The attribution end-to-end test is invoked as `run_case(\"G3\", ...)`, while the repro uses a spec name (`run_case(\"plan-review-G7\", ...)`). The plan does not say which spec name drives a G3 container case through the criterion arm, or what FakeRunner findings are injected.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f765205d0742f159b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — attribution bullet","norm_id":"nc7f3ba0568ab1fbf","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor passes \"G3\" and `_criterion_id` does not resolve a bare id, so the test errors.","The executor uses plan-review-container and hits 'no eval solver'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how `register_contracts()` idempotency works (a registry-presence check vs a module flag). Have the scorer fail if `response_model_for` returns the review_result model, and add `passes.py` to Scope if re-registration needs a change.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"calls `passes.register_contracts()` (idempotent, `passes.py:120`) before `contracts.response_model_for(...)`, so it never falls back to the review_result model (`contracts.py:38-40`)\"","Test: \"removes `plan_review_findings` from the contract registry ... asserts it passes and that the contract is registered again\"","Scope lists only eval_scorers.py and two test files."],"finding":"Self-registration assumes `passes.register_contracts()` re-registers the contract after it has been removed from the registry. If its idempotency is implemented as a module-level 'already registered' flag, the fresh-interpreter test fails, and `response_model_for` silently falls back to the review_result model. The fix would then need an edit to `passes.py`, which is outside the declared Scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3e7c5192b5251b15","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1; Testing — self-registration bullet; Scope","norm_id":"n93a8842219c6e234","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["register_contracts guards on a flag set at import. After the test deletes the registry entry, the call is a no-op and the scorer validates against review_result again."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"After registering, have the scorer check that `contracts.response_model_for(\"plan_review_findings\")` is not the review_result fallback model, and return a failing score with an explicit 'contract not registered' message if it is.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a criterion (or a documented rationale) for confirming that an `eval-live` / `run_eval` run of the seven specs reports no `review result failed schema validation` errors, or extend the happy-path FakeRunner findings to a full Pass-1 field set.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Problem: \"In the live prompt-eval loop (`run_eval` per dataset-bearing spec, `eval-live` job ...) seven plan-review criterion specs fail\"","Every acceptance criterion is offline or unit-level; none mentions eval-live or a live re-run, and none states why one is unnecessary."],"finding":"The problem is defined by the live `eval-live` loop, but no criterion re-runs it, and no rationale is given for omitting a live check. FakeRunner findings are minimal (`finding` + `criteria`), so they may not reflect the full field set a live model emits through normalization.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1551dfd1fb7dcf0f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria; Problem","norm_id":"n3c47a0700720e91d","priority":0.1571,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Normalized live findings carry a field or type the `_pass1_model` rejects. The offline tests pass, but eval-live still reports schema failures (with a different message)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reset every acceptance criterion to `- [ ]` until its named test or `make verify` actually passes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E1","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"- [x] `emits_valid_findings` validates the `plan_review_findings` contract ...\" — and the same `[x]` on every AC, including \"- [x] `make verify` exits 0.\""],"finding":"All five acceptance criteria are already marked `[x]` before any implementation exists. This misstates completion status.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe00a98bd9a81e1be","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Cri